    <string name="about_heading">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Arcalume %1$s for Android</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Arcalume does not request internet access. Photos, vaults and the custody log are stored only in this app\'s private storage and are excluded from cloud backups. Nothing leaves the phone unless you export it.</string>
    <string name="limits_heading">What Arcalume can\'t do</string>
    <string name="limit_1">Text inside a blown-out glare spot is gone from the photo. Arcalume fills that area smoothly and marks it; it never invents characters. Retake the photo at an angle instead.</string>
    <string name="limit_2">The custody log proves that records were not changed after sealing. It can\'t prove what happened to a photo before it reached Arcalume, and it is not a certification that evidence is admissible.</string>
    <string name="limit_3">Reading order is geometry: it finds columns and blocks. It does not read or understand the text.</string>
